\section{Episode boundaries and observation flags}{

\strong{Left truncation.} For individuals born before the simulation
starts, the first episode begins at the simulation start and has
\code{statusEntry = 0}: entry into their initial state was not observed
during the simulation. For individuals born on or after the start
date, the first episode begins at birth and has \code{statusEntry = 1}.

\strong{Immigrants.} With \code{migr = TRUE}, an immigrant's first episode begins
on their arrival date rather than at the start of observation, and
counts as observed. Their earlier life happened elsewhere and is
outside the study.

\strong{Right censoring.} Anyone who has neither entered an absorbing state
nor already got a censored row gets one more episode, running from
their last transition to the end of observation: the end of the
simulation, or the day they reach \code{maxAge} if that comes first. The
simulation stops putting a person at risk at \verb{maxAge - 0.01 years},
}

